/P 905 0 R
/E (This book did not come from a moment of inspiration, but from a long series of choices. Some good, some wrong. The difference between them was not talent, luck or context, but how I chose to continue when it became difficult. This book does not promise definitive answers, nor does it claim to offer a universally valid recipe. It does not matter how motivated you are in a day, but how disciplined you remain in the days when you are no longer in the mood. This book was born out of this reality. You won't find complicated theories or quick promises here. You will find direct observations, lessons learned through practice and a personal experiment carried out to the end. Personal development is not presented as a beautiful concept, but as a sometimes uncomfortable process that requires perseverance, self-control and assumption. I wrote this book for those who understood that change does not come from the outside, but from small decisions made consistently. For those who know that discipline beats motivation and that success is the result of a trained mindset, not a lucky moment. If these pages will make you ask yourself more questions about your own habits, how you manage your time and how much you are willing to insist, then the book has reached its goal. Because, in the end, it is not the circumstances that define your path, but the attitude with which you face them. The personal journey described here is not filtered to impress, but to reflect the authenticity of the transformation.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
