1121 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 906 0 R
/E (   They wake up, rush through their days, chase noise, approval, money, and momentum without ever asking themselves where they are actually going. They mistake movement for progress and exhaustion for purpose. They confuse visibility with value. I was one of them. For a long time, I believed that success was loud. That it needed to be proven, displayed, validated. I believed that freedom was something external, I thought that if I could just row harder, faster, farther, I would eventually outrun uncertainty, fear, and doubt. I was wrong. Because no matter how far you travel on the surface, you carry yourself with you. And if your mind is restless, your life will be too. This book is not about escaping life. It is about diving into it.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
