1228 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 921 0 R
/E (Not because you suddenly became more motivated, but because routine creates pressure, and pressure demands adjustment. That adjustment, repeated daily, is discipline forming in real time.)
/Pg 26 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
1229 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 921 0 R
/E (     This is how discipline actually grows: through small, structured inconveniences that force you to prioritize what matters. One hour earlier in the morning. One less distraction at night. One deliberate decision repeated long enough to become automatic. We often speak about discipline as if it were something we eventually reach, a final state where effort becomes effortless and consistency no longer requires intention. In reality, discipline is never finished. It is not a destination, but a continuous process of adjustment, repetition, and refinement. We are always in a process of disciplining ourselves, whether consciously or unconsciously. Every choice we make either strengthens structure or weakens it. Every routine we follow trains us into becoming a certain type of person, even when we are not actively thinking about it.)
/Pg 26 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
