1342 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 939 0 R
/E (       The human brain has a limited working memory, and multitasking overloads it quickly. When we try to do multiple cognitive tasks at once, the brain cannot retain information efficiently, resulting in forgetfulness, errors, and incomplete learning. For instance, attempting to study for an exam while watching TV or replying to messages prevents the brain from encoding information into long-term memory. Studies confirm that repeated multitasking reduces retention and comprehension. In contrast, concentrating fully on one task at a time allows the brain to process, store, and recall information effectively. This is why focused study sessions outperform chaotic, split-attention sessions every time. Memory, understanding, and deep learning thrive on undivided attention.)
/Pg 44 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
