/P 948 0 R
/E (       Emotional instability is often mistaken for sensitivity or personality, but in many cases it is the result of disorganized living. Discipline introduces rhythm, and rhythm creates calm. When your days follow a structure, your nervous system responds with predictability rather than anxiety.)
/Pg 53 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
1406 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 948 0 R
/E (      Discipline reduces the number of decisions you must make daily, conserving mental energy. This allows emotions to exist without controlling behavior. You feel tired, but you act. You feel resistance, but you continue. Over time, this separation between feeling and action builds emotional maturity. Rather than suppressing emotions, discipline contains them. It provides a framework within which emotions can be processed safely. This is why disciplined individuals often appear calmer not because they feel less, but because they are not governed by what they feel. )
/Pg 53 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
1407 0 obj
<<
