1429 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 951 0 R
/E ( True discipline recognizes that life is dynamic. Energy fluctuates, circumstances change, and unexpected challenges arise. A disciplined approach does not ignore these realities; it integrates them. Instead of forcing consistency at all costs, discipline focuses on continuity. Missing a day does not erase momentum. Pausing does not equal quitting. This perspective preserves long-term progress by preventing burnout and discouragement.)
/Pg 56 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
1430 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 951 0 R
/E (     Discipline also creates space for recovery and reflection. Rest becomes intentional rather than accidental. Reflection allows recalibration without self-judgment. Over time, this balance strengthens resilience. Discipline stops draining energy and begins conserving it. Rather than exhausting the individual, it builds endurance. True discipline is not about relentless intensity; it is about the ability to continue with clarity, stability, and purpose over extended periods of time.)
/Pg 56 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
1431 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
