1432 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 951 0 R
/E (      Confidence rooted in results is fragile because it depends on circumstances, external validation, and fleeting successes. When outcomes are inconsistent or unexpected, this kind of confidence crumbles. Confidence rooted in discipline, however, is different. It is durable, grounded in repeated proof that you can rely on yourself regardless of what happens outside. Every time you follow through on a commitment, even when motivation fades or distractions arise, you are building evidence that you can be trusted by yourself. This internal trust is the foundation of genuine confidence.)
/Pg 56 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
1433 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 951 0 R
/E (      This confidence is calm, quiet, and deeply personal. It does not demand applause or recognition because it is earned through action rather than approval. It grows in the small, often overlooked moments: when you wake up early despite fatigue, when you finish a task you had been avoiding, when you say no to a temptation that conflicts with your goals. Each of these choices reinforces the understanding that you are capable, reliable, and in control of your own life. )
/Pg 56 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
