1448 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 954 0 R
/E (     We often say that we live in the age of information, but what we rarely admit is that we are also living in the age of exhaustion, where knowing more does not necessarily mean understanding more, and being connected all the time does not mean being present at all. Digital literacy today is no longer about knowing how to use technology, because almost everyone does; it is about knowing when not to use it, when to step back, when to refuse constant stimulation, and when to protect your attention as if it were something fragile and irreplaceable, because in truth, it is.)
/Pg 59 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
1449 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
