/P 954 0 R
/E (     Discipline in this context becomes an act of self-respect. It is the quiet decision to not let algorithms dictate your emotional state, to not let endless scrolling replace thinking, and to not confuse consumption with growth. When discipline is missing, technology trains us to live on the surface of things, jumping from idea to idea without ever staying long enough to be changed by any of them. When discipline is present, technology becomes useful instead of intrusive, supportive instead of addictive, and suddenly attention turns from a weakness into a skill that can be trained, refined, and protected.)
/Pg 59 0 R
/K [3]
