/E (      Discipline rarely feels rewarding at the beginning, and one of the first things people notice when they start changing their habits is not progress, but distance. Distance from routines that once felt comfortable, from environments that no longer match who they are becoming, and sometimes even from people who shared the old version of their life. This distance can feel uncomfortable and, at times, deeply lonely, because it removes familiar reference points and replaces them with uncertainty rather than immediate results.)
/Pg 62 0 R
/K [2]
