/E (       Discipline is often misunderstood as something rigid or severe, as if it were an act of constant pressure applied to the present self, but when looked at honestly, discipline is one of the most compassionate choices a person can make. It is not about denying yourself comfort for the sake of suffering, but about recognizing that every decision made today quietly shapes the conditions in which you will live tomorrow. Discipline is, in essence, an agreement with your future self, a promise that you will not leave them to deal with chaos, regret, or preventable consequences alone.)
/Pg 63 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
1482 0 obj
