/E (      Every person is responsible for what they build inside. Some people let their lives be shaped by external pressure, trends, and noise. Others decide to pay attention to their own structure. Discipline is what allows you to build that structure step by step. It helps you decide how you spend your days, what habits you keep, and what values guide your choices. This is where The Underwater Kingdom truly exists, not at the surface where everything is fast and temporary, but below, where things grow slowly and last longer. What you build there becomes stable. Discipline is the path downward, and those who choose it discover that real freedom does not come from reacting to the world, but from being grounded enough to move through it on their own terms.)
/Pg 64 0 R
/K [5]
