/E (      Discipline rarely survives in isolation for long periods of time, not because the individual is weak, but because humans are shaped continuously by the environment in which they choose to remain. The people around us influence not only what we do, but how normal or abnormal our effort feels, and this perception quietly determines whether discipline becomes sustainable or exhausting.)
/Pg 68 0 R
/K [4]
