/P 963 0 R
/E (      When individuals are surrounded by people who share similar values, ambitions, and standards, discipline stops feeling like resistance against the world and starts feeling like alignment with it. In such environments, focus is respected rather than questioned, consistency is understood rather than mocked, and effort is not mistaken for obsession. This shared vision creates a psychological safety where discipline can grow without constant self-justification. Humans unconsciously synchronize habits, language, and expectations with those they spend the most time with. When discipline is present in the social environment, it becomes reinforced rather than challenged. )
