/E ( Calm is confused with detachment, and self-control is mistaken for suppression. Within The Underwater Kingdom, this misunderstanding marks the divide between surface life and depth. At the surface, value is assigned to what is loud, visible, and shared. Below it, value is built through consistency, restraint, and quiet intention. Disciplined people live closer to that depth, which makes their choices difficult to read from above. )
/Pg 71 0 R
/K [1]
>>
