/E (     Ultimately, disciplined people are misunderstood because they are operating by a different logic. Their actions are guided less by approval and more by alignment. They are not trying to appear disciplined; they are trying to live sustainably. And while misunderstanding may be the cost of that choice, the clarity and freedom it brings are often worth far more than being easily understood.)
/Pg 71 0 R
/K [2]
>>
