/E ( It does not excuse harm or ignore boundaries, but it acknowledges that every interaction teaches something. Discipline allows you to extract the lesson without carrying the resentment. Gratitude toward others also protects relationships over time. Disciplined communication prevents words from being driven solely by emotion, and gratitude softens the space between people. When appreciation is expressed consistently, even in small and quiet ways, it builds trust and reduces unnecessary conflict. Many relationships fail not because of major betrayals, but because appreciation was never verbalized.)
