1596 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 977 0 R
/E (    Discipline is not only about persistence and endurance, it is also about knowing when to shift focus, when to stop investing time, effort, or emotions in one direction, and channel them somewhere more productive. Know we will dive deeper into a subject that we discussed about it earlier. Many people equate discipline with stubbornness, thinking that staying the course no matter what is the mark of self-control. In reality, true discipline requires judgment, self-awareness, and the courage to redirect energy when the current path no longer serves growth.)
/Pg 82 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
1597 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 977 0 R
/E (    Consider a student pouring hours into a project that consistently yields poor results. Without reflection, the time and energy spent can become wasted effort. Redirecting focus toward areas where progress is achievable like building skills that complement their strengths or collaborating with someone who can elevate their work demonstrates mature discipline. It is not quitting; it is strategic action. Learning to distinguish between persistence and misapplied effort is a skill few master, but it defines high performers across any field.)
/Pg 82 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
1598 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 977 0 R
/E <>
/Pg 82 0 R
