endobj
1599 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 977 0 R
/E (Athletes, entrepreneurs, and artists all practice this principle intuitively. A runner might shift focus from a race that cannot realistically be won to training for a future event where success is attainable. An entrepreneur may pause a failing venture to pursue a more promising opportunity. An artist may abandon a piece that no longer aligns with their vision to pour energy into a creation that better expresses their voice. In each case, discipline is about allocating effort wisely to maximize growth, impact, and fulfillment.)
/Pg 82 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
