1605 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 978 0 R
/E (      Discipline is not only about doing the right things consistently it is also about choosing what deserves your attention and passion. In a world flooded with endless options, distractions, and shiny new opportunities, knowing how to filter your interests becomes a form of discipline in itself. Without this filtering, energy is scattered, focus is lost, and growth slows. Learning to prioritize what truly matters is what separates those who make progress from those who remain busy but stagnant.)
/Pg 83 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
1606 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 978 0 R
/E (      Imagine your mind as a garden of interests. Each curiosity or hobby is a seed, but you cannot nurture them all equally. Some will flourish, some will fade, and some may even compete with the growth of others. Discipline requires identifying which interests align with your values, goals, and long-term vision, and then devoting your energy to nurturing them while letting go of the rest. )
/Pg 83 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
