1636 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 984 0 R
/E (    One of the most overlooked forms of discipline is the ability to meet challenges with dignity rather than reacting impulsively in the heat of the moment. Life constantly places obstacles in front of us. Some are small and irritating, others feel unfair or deeply personal. The difference between growth and stagnation often lies not in what happens to us, but in how we choose to respond when pressure appears.)
/Pg 89 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
1637 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 984 0 R
/E (    Overreaction usually feels justified in the moment. )
/Pg 89 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
