/E (   The discipline of removing background noise is not an annual cleaning marathon. It is the daily ritual of making your bed, washing your dishes, and taking out your mental trash. You do it because you know that tomorrow morning you will start from a clean slate. And from that clean background, you will truly be able to build what you desire without having to turn the volume all the way up to cover a buzzing unease. There, in that chosen silence, you find the freedom to hear your own voice and to act in accordance with it. When the background finally settles, life does not become louder or faster. It becomes cleaner. And in that clean space, purpose has room to breathe.)
/Pg 94 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
