/E (Disciplined rest happens on a micro-scale throughout the day. The popular Pomodoro Technique \(25 minutes work, 5-minute break\) is a start, but more advanced research suggests the 52/17 Rule: working with deep focus for about 52 minutes, followed by a complete break of about 17 minutes. This break is not for checking email. It is for standing, stretching, looking out a window, walking, or deep breathing. These rhythmic pauses prevent cognitive fatigue, maintain a high level of performance throughout the day, and stave off the need for massive recovery later.)
/Pg 99 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
