<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 994 0 R
/E (     Discipline is often framed as a solitary pursuit: the lone runner at dawn, the scholar burning midnight oil, the artist facing the blank canvas alone. This is a romantic but incomplete picture. While the commitment must be yours alone, the environment in which that commitment is nurtured is collective. You are not a sealed fortress, you are a permeable organism, constantly exchanging energy, ideas, and emotion with the people around you. Your discipline, therefore, is not just what you do in isolation, but what you allow and cultivate in your relational space. The most profound and challenging discipline may well be the conscious, courageous selection of your inner circle. It is the discipline of tending to the social soil in which your character and dreams are meant to grow. )
/Pg 99 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
1726 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 994 0 R
/E (     One of the most influential and underestimated forms of discipline is the decision to choose the people you allow close to you. )
/Pg 99 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
