/E (     When you refuse to give a process its necessary time, you are not demonstrating admirable drive; you are attempting to force a harvest from unripe soil. You produce the superficial facsimile of a result: the hastily written book, the forced relationship, the business launched before its foundation is solid, which inevitably crumbles under the slightest pressure because its roots are shallow. The discipline of time is, therefore, a discipline of integrity. It is a covenant with your future self to build something that lasts, not just something that appears.)
