1809 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1008 0 R
/E (    We arrive now at the summit of inner discipline. If all previous disciplines have been about building your circle, your mindset, your schedule, this one is about the profound and difficult art of demolition. Not demolition of another, but of the internal prison you have built around a past hurt. There is a form of discipline that feels heavier than waking up early, harder than consistency, and far more uncomfortable than effort. It is the discipline of forgiveness. Not because it excuses what happened, but because it refuses to let the past sit at the steering wheel of your future.)
/Pg 113 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
