/P 1009 0 R
/T (Strength here is not about power over others, but mastery over yourself. Forgiveness is, purely and powerfully, a strategic decision for your own peace and progress. It is the ultimate act of reclaiming your energy. When you hold onto resentment, you are perpetually renting space in your mind to a past event and the person who caused it. You are allowing them to live there, rent-free, diverting your emotional resources, your focus, and your creative power. As Tyler Perry so pointedly observes, "When you haven't forgiven those who have hurt you, you turn back against your future. When you do forgive, you start walking forward." Unforgiveness chains you to a past you cannot change, forcing you to face backwards while life moves on.)
/E (Strength here is not about power over others, but mastery over yourself. Forgiveness is, purely and powerfully, a strategic decision for your own peace and progress. It is the ultimate act of reclaiming your energy. When you hold onto resentment, you are perpetually renting space in your mind to a past event and the person who caused it. You are allowing them to live there, rent-free, diverting your emotional resources, your focus, and your creative power. As Tyler Perry so pointedly observes, "When you haven't forgiven those who have hurt you, you turn back against your future. When you do forgive, you start walking forward." Unforgiveness chains you to a past you cannot change, forcing you to face backwards while life moves on.)
