/E (   Many people unknowingly use money to compensate for things they have not yet built within themselves. They use it to buy confidence, to mask insecurity, to prove value, or to earn approval. But money cannot do inner work. It can only expose what is missing. When money is used as a substitute for identity, it becomes heavy, when it is used as a tool aligned with identity, it becomes light.)
/Pg 120 0 R
/K [4]
>>
