1973 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1028 0 R
/E (   People who struggle to save are often told they lack discipline, but sometimes the issue runs deeper. If someone does not believe they deserve security, saving feels pointless. If someone lives in constant urgency, planning ahead feels unnatural. Saving requires the belief that you are worth caring for beyond today. This is why saving is not about how much you put aside, but about the habit of choosing yourself repeatedly, even when no immediate reward is visible. Each saved amount becomes a quiet affirmation that you are not living only for survival, but for continuity. Saving also creates psychological freedom. It reduces fear-based decisions. It allows choice rather than reaction. It transforms emergencies into inconveniences and dreams into possibilities. Over time, this sense of preparedness builds confidence that no purchase could ever replace.)
/Pg 133 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
