/P 1029 0 R
/E (    We don't just buy a product, we buy a promised emotion. Advertising doesn't sell a car, it sells freedom. It doesn't sell a perfume, it sells attraction. This is how the mechanism works in our brain: we see an object, the brain anticipates dopamine \(the pleasure of the purchase and status\), and the prefrontal cortex \(responsible for reason and control\) is overwhelmed. We buy to fill emotional voids of boredom, loneliness, anxiety, or insecurity. It's a quick form of "sales therapy.")
/Pg 134 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
