2112 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1043 0 R
/E (    Your environment is a mirror of your mind. A chaotic desk breeds chaotic thoughts; a cluttered kitchen induces low-grade stress. The goal is not a showroom, but a default state of "just enough order" that feels neutral, not oppressive. To achieve this, you institute a rule so simple it requires almost no thought: The Five-Minute Evening Reset.)
/Pg 148 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
2113 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1043 0 R
/E (    This is not a cleaning marathon. It is a daily ritual of returning things to their designed positions. As the last act of your workday, you set a timer for five minutes. You put the coffee mug in the dishwasher. You file the two loose papers. You straighten the monitor and keyboard.)
/Pg 148 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
