/P 1044 0 R
/E ( You wipe the counter, place the book back on the shelf, you are not cleaning for the sake of cleanliness, you are resetting the stage for your future self. You are guaranteeing that tomorrow morning, you will not be greeted by the visual noise of yesterday's entropy. When you are adrift, this custodial act, performed nightly on autopilot, ensures that your physical space does not become another source of overwhelm. It remains a passive, orderly container for your turbulent mind.)
/Pg 149 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
2117 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1044 0 R
/E (    A drifting mind is a haunted mind. It loops on anxieties, half-remembered tasks, and fragments of ideas. Trying to "clear your mind" through force is impossible. Instead, you must build a reliable external system that your mind trusts implicitly. This system has two parts, and they must be dead simple.)
/Pg 149 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
2118 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1044 0 R
/E (First, The Designated Worry Pad. This is a specific, physical notebook or a single digital note titled "Braindump." Its rule is sacred: anything that feels urgent, nagging, or circular in your mind gets written here, with zero judgment or immediate action required. "Call dentist." "What if project fails?" "Need gift for Mom." The moment it is written, you have permission to mentally release it. The custodian has received the memo. The system now holds the worry, so your mind doesn't have to. When you are clear-headed, you review it. When you are adrift, you simply dump and forget, trusting the capture.)
/Pg 149 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
2119 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1044 0 R
/E (     Second, The Unambiguous Next Action. For the few truly non-negotiable items \(pay the tax bill, email your boss\), you practice ruthless simplification. You do not write "Taxes" on a list. That is a dark cloud of undefined dread. You define the very next, physical action. "Find the login document in the 'Finance' folder." That is a task so specific and small that even a depleted brain can latch onto it. You are not asking your adrift self to solve a puzzle, you are asking it to perform a single, obviously. The system has done the thinking in advance, breaking the mountain into a single, passable stone.)
/Pg 149 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
