/P 1046 0 R
/E (Instead, the moment your feet touch the floor, you perform a single, conscious act of embodiment. Walk to a window. Place your hands on the sill if you can. Look outside. See the colour of the sky. See a single tree, a rooftop, a parked car. Notice one single, mundane detail, the way the light hits a puddle, the slow sway of a branch. Breathe in through your nose, out through your mouth, three times. You are not meditating; you are simply reminding your animal body that it is here, on a planet, in a room, and not lost in the digital ether.)
/Pg 151 0 R
/K [2]
