2148 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1047 0 R
/E (     Modern existence is a processor running at maximum capacity. Projects, deadlines, logistical worries, and an endless stream of micro-decisions consume all your mental resources. In this context, the most important connections those with your partner, children, close friends, family, don't break from some major dispute. They slowly dry up through simple omissions. Through evenings where everyone is physically present but mentally miles away. Through weekends that slip away managing tasks, without a moment of authentic contact. Love is not just a feeling. It is a resource that requires an allocation of attention and time. And when life becomes chaotic, this resource is the first to be diverted to "crisis mode." Relational engineering is the practice of treating connections as vital infrastructure. You don't let the water or power grid work only when you feel like it or when it breaks.)
/Pg 152 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
