2161 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1049 0 R
/E (     Procrastination is not a character flaw. It's a predictable symptom. It is the pain-avoidance mechanism of a brain confronted with a task that signals one of three things: Boredom, Uncertainty, or Threat. The vague, daunting task on your list "Write report," "Plan project," "Do taxes" is a cognitive monster. Your brain looks at it and sees a dark, shapeless cave. It doesn't know where the entrance is, what's inside, how long it will take, or if there are monsters lurking. So it does the rational thing: it avoids the cave. It chooses the immediate, certain pleasure of scrolling, cleaning, or "planning to plan" over the perceived pain of that ambiguous void.)
/Pg 154 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
2162 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1049 0 R
/E (     The classic advice "Just get started!" is useless. Starting is the problem. The Anti-Procrastination System bypasses the need for heroic willpower. It doesn't ask you to confront the cave. It teaches you to dismantle the cave, brick by brick, until all that's left is a single, harmless brick on the path. And then it builds a path so frictionless you'd trip over it if you tried to avoid it.)
/Pg 154 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
