2183 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1052 0 R
/E (This is the Brutal First Action from the Anti-Procrastination system, applied to the crisis. Broken: A critical work deadline was missed. Next Action: Draft a 2-sentence email to the client: "I have missed the deadline. I am outlining my recovery plan and will send it by EOD tomorrow. My apologies." Do not solve it. Just stop the bleed. What is the SMALLEST PIECE of my old routine that would feel right? Not the full morning routine. Just drinking your coffee from your favorite mug, by the window, for two minutes. Not the full workout. Just putting on your running shoes and walking to the mailbox. You are not rebuilding the system. You are searching for one familiar wire to reconnect, to send a trickle charge back into your psyche.)
/Pg 157 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
2184 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1052 0 R
/E (     This manual is not a hack to bypass pain or to maintain productivity during tragedy. It is a containment vessel. Its purpose is to prevent a crisis from spiraling into a catastrophe, and to protect the core of you, your health, your key relationships, your basic stability while the storm passes.)
/Pg 157 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
2185 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1052 0 R
/E (A system that cannot weather a crash is a brittle toy. A life that includes a manual for the crashes is a resilient one. The true test of your engineering is not whether the systems run perfectly in calm seas, but whether they include a waterproof, beacon-lit, well-provisioned lifeboat for when the ship is going down. And the wisdom to know that sometimes, for a while, the lifeboat is the ship. Climb in, seal the hatch, and ride out the storm. )
/Pg 157 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
