2190 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1053 0 R
/E (     This is the trap: motivation gives the illusion of progress before any real progress has been made.)
/Pg 158 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
2191 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1053 0 R
/E (Motivation is emotional by nature, it depends on mood, energy, validation, and circumstances. On good days, it feels powerful, on bad days, it disappears completely. When we rely on motivation, we unknowingly tie our growth to how we feel and feelings are unstable. They change with sleep, stress, disappointment, and even the weather. A life built on motivation alone is a life built on something fragile. Another reason motivation traps us is that it makes beginnings feel more important than continuity. We celebrate starting. New notebooks, new plans, new routines. But discipline and systems care very little about how inspired you feel at the start. Motivation loves intensity. Growth requires endurance.)
/Pg 158 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
