/E (     Emerson masterfully frames our emotional experience as a transaction, an economy of the spirit. In this ledger, anger, resentment, and offense are not mere feelings,  they are investments with devastatingly negative returns. The currency is our most precious and non-renewable resource: the present moment. To choose anger is to consciously, minute by minute, divest yourself of serenity. It is a real-time payment of peace for poison, a voluntary forfeiture of the only time we ever truly own, now.)
/Pg 162 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
