/E (Children feel and react. Adults feel and choose. An emotionally disciplined person does not deny their feelings. They acknowledge them fully, sometimes painfully, but they do not outsource control to them. They understand that emotions are data, not commands. Anger might be data telling you a boundary was crossed. Fear might be data warning you of uncertainty. Sadness might be data signaling loss or unmet needs. But data must be analyzed, not blindly executed.)
/Pg 165 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
2251 0 obj
<<
