/E (     Think of a pilot flying through turbulence. Panic would be a feeling. Grabbing random controls would be a reaction. Training teaches pilots to feel the fear, acknowledge it, and still follow procedure. Emotional control works the same way. The goal is not calm at all costs, it is clarity under pressure.)
/Pg 165 0 R
/K [6]
>>
