/E (     Each time you pause instead of explode, you are rewiring your nervous system. Each time you choose response over reaction, you reclaim authority over your life. Each time you separate who you are from what you feel, you become harder to manipulate by others and by your own impulses. When you stop bleeding energy, you regain direction. And when your actions are no longer ruled by emotional storms, you begin to move forward with intention, not impulse. Feeling is human. Responding wisely is strength.)
/Pg 166 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
2257 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 1061 0 R
/T (The Anatomy of an Emotional Wave)
/E (The Anatomy of an Emotional Wave)
/Pg 166 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
2258 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1061 0 R
/E (      Let us understand, for a moment, a fundamental truth: an emotion is not a verdict, not a flaw, not a rupture in reality. It is a wave. And like any wave, it has a point of ascent, an overwhelming crest, and then, inevitably, a retreat. To experience an intense emotion be it fear, anger, a thrill of joy, or a fog of anguish  is to be caught in the heart of an interior natural force. But just as an oceanographer does not drown while studying waves, but rather measures, charts, and predicts them, we too can learn to navigate the waters of our own psychic ocean, if we understand the anatomy of this transient phenomenon.)
/Pg 166 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
2259 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1061 0 R
/E (    Let us begin with the first spark, the almost imperceptible Trigger. This is not necessarily a failure or a tragedy. Often, it is something far more subtle: a tone of voice, a precisely chosen word, a memory, a physical sensation, a shadow passing the window. It is a signal that, passing through the filters of brains trained by millions of years of evolution to detect danger and opportunity, strikes an internal alarm bell. Here, in the depths of the limbic system, in the amygdala this small almond of neural tissue that is our eternal, alarmed emotional guardian, a fire ignites. Not a fire of rational thought, but of primitive feeling. It is a fire alarm that completely bypasses the quiet office of the prefrontal cortex, where we analyze and weigh. )
/Pg 166 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
2260 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1061 0 R
/E (The underwater kingdom)
/Pg 166 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
