>>
endobj
2262 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1062 0 R
/E (This signal shouts, directly and without censorship: Danger! or Joy! or Loss!. And here, the wave begins to form, entering its phase of Cognitive Amplification. Our mind, this tireless factory of stories and interpretations, gets to work. It takes the spark and begins to pour gasoline over it. Thoughts line up like a narrative choir, rapid, automatic, often distorted: "He said that because he despises me," "Now the worst will surely happen," "I will never escape this." This internal story which psychologists call "self-talk" or "automatic thoughts" is the supreme wave-builder. It transforms a raw sensation into a personal narrative, giving it meaning, context, and, most importantly, an escalating dramatic quality. Each thought is like a wind pulling across the water's surface, raising the wave's crest higher, more threateningly.)
/Pg 167 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
2263 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1062 0 R
/E (    As the narrative grows, your physical body, this incredible instrument of sensitivity, embodies the emotion. This is the phase of Somatic Incarnation. The wave is no longer just an idea or a story; it becomes living matter. The autonomic nervous system, this automatic pilot of vital functions, takes command.)
/Pg 167 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
2264 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1062 0 R
/E (Then comes The Crest. The peak moment, when the wave seems all-powerful, impenetrable. It is the state where the feeling occupies the entire horizon of consciousness. Rational thoughts, the calm voice of reason, seem like a whisper drowned out by the roar of the wave. You feel that this feeling is all that you are and all that you will ever be. Here lies the final illusion of emotion: the illusion of permanence. It whispers, or shouts, that this state is definitive, that it will never pass, that you are the rage, are the panic, are the despair. It is a betrayal of the mind, a trick of perception at its most overwhelming moment. But even at this crest, the wave reaches its climax. Its energy begins, inevitably, to be consumed.)
/Pg 167 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
2265 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1062 0 R
/E (     And so we enter the final phase, that of Dissolution and Withdrawal. )
/Pg 167 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
