/E (You are allowed to protect your mornings from disaster to refuse to let algorithms dictate your emotional state to choose calm without guilt. Calm is not escape it is a form of resistance in a noisy world Inner stability is not detachment from reality it is the strength to face it without losing yourself. Because only a clear mind can truly help. Only an emotionally regulated person can build something good in the world In an age of constant crisis emotional control is no longer a luxury it is a responsibility to yourself and to others.)
/Pg 174 0 R
