/E (    Collective emotions have a strange power, because when we are in a crowd, fear and anger no longer belong solely to us; they become a shared current that can sweep through everyone in sight. Suddenly, personal judgment feels slippery and unreliable. Studies in social psychology show that emotions are contagious through subtle cues like posture, tone of voice, and facial expression, which means that when one person panics, others often follow, even without fully understanding why.)
/Pg 176 0 R
