/E (The key is to notice the emotion as it arises, to name it internally, and to create a tiny gap between perception and reaction. Neuroscientists note that mirror neurons amplify social emotional signals, so being mindful of your internal state acts as a stabilizer for your nervous system. It is a discipline to feel the shared tension without being carried away. It is learning to ride a wave without being submerged. And when practiced consistently, this ability becomes a form of resilience, allowing you to respond thoughtfully even when everyone else reacts impulsively. It teaches that freedom from collective waves is not isolation, but skillful engagement that honors both your humanity and the humanity around you.)
/Pg 177 0 R
/K [1]
>>
