/P 1076 0 R
/E (    The impact of practicing the witness mind is profound: athletes maintain peak performance without being derailed by anxiety, doctors save lives without panic interfering, creatives produce work that is focused and intentional even under pressure, and anyone who applies these principles to daily life discovers a new freedom from the tyranny of reaction. In essence, this discipline transforms the internal landscape from a reactive series of emotional spikes and crashes into a steady, coherent rhythm where the individual remains in control of their thoughts, actions, and emotional energy. It is a cornerstone of emotional resilience and a practical demonstration of how discipline, when applied to the inner world, can create stability, freedom, and enduring strength.)
/Pg 181 0 R
/K [3]
>>
