/E (    Taleb advocates for a barbell approach: place 90% of your capital \(time, energy, identity\) in ultra-safe, stable, serene pursuits \(the foundation\), and 10% in highly speculative, high-volatility experiments \(the exploration\). This creates asymmetric upside: minimal downside risk if the experiment fails, life-altering upside if it succeeds.)
/Pg 194 0 R
/K [7]
