/E (Maintain your stable career \(the safe side\) while dedicating 10% of your weekly hours to a bold, risky creative project, a speculative skill, or an "antifragile hobby" with unpredictable outcomes \(e.g., writing a novel, building an open-source tool, learning improvisational theater\). The small, contained failures in the 10% zone make you smarter and more adaptable without threatening your foundation.)
/Pg 195 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
2505 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1090 0 R
/E (     Cultivate the "Emotional Portfolio" so that a blow to your professional self-concept is absorbed by your identity as a mentor, an artist, or a community member. Build skill redundancy, learn adjacent skills so you are not rendered obsolete by a single technological shift. This creates optionality in your own being, allowing you to pivot and reconfigure. Systematically identify and eliminate single points of failure in your life: the debt that makes you dependent on a job you hate, the toxic relationship that monopolizes your emotional energy, the rigid belief that you are only "you" if you follow one specific path. Each subtraction reduces your exposure to catastrophic harm and increases your freedom to engage with volatility from a position of strength.)
/Pg 195 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
2506 0 obj
