/S /P
/P 1094 0 R
/E (     An enduring name is built on a paradox: it must be deeply specific in its foundation, yet universally resonant in its application. It is not built on being everything to everyone, but on being one profound thing to the right someone. Your name becomes attached not to a fleeting topic, but to a timeless function. The carpenter is not known for "wood trends," but for the creation of shelter and beauty from raw material.)
/Pg 199 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
