/P 1095 0 R
/E (     To outlive trends does not mean to ignore them, it means to engage with them from a position of unassailable strength.)
/Pg 200 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
2543 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1095 0 R
/E (Allow a trend to illuminate a new facet of your "one hard thing." If your domain is leadership, examine a social media trend through the lens of influence psychology, not to become a social media guru, but to deepen your timeless study of authority and connection. When everyone is frantically chasing the next thing, your steadfast focus on your core mission becomes a signal of sanity. You become a refuge for those exhausted by the churn, attracting an audience that values depth over distraction. A trend is a stress test for your philosophy. Does it hold up? Does it offer a more meaningful explanation? The process of pressure-testing your ideas against the fad of the day only serves to strengthen and refine them.)
/Pg 200 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
2544 0 obj
<<
