/S /P
/P 1095 0 R
/E (     When your name becomes an adjective, you have achieved the ultimate: you have moved beyond being a person commenting on a field, to having defined a category of thought or action. You are no longer in the race. You have become part of the landscape. Building such a name is the work of a lifetime. It is forged in the stubborn refusal to be derivative, the courage to be profoundly specific, and the patience to let credibility compound in silence. It is the art of becoming an institution of one, a reference point that stands firm as the tides of trend and opinion wash endlessly against it, only to recede, leaving your foundation unmarked and your name, unmistakably, your own.)
/Pg 200 0 R
/K [5]
>>
