/E (You depart with dignity, expressing thanks for what was learned or shared, without theatrics or blame. "This path is no longer the right one for me, and I wish you the very best." The message is clear, but the structure remains. The door is closed, but not welded shut. Sometimes, the most powerful action is deliberate inaction. You simply stop investing energy. You let the connection go dormant without a dramatic pronouncement. The bridge remains, unused, but it can be cleared if a future, unforeseen necessity arises. You acknowledge the relationship is over in its current form, but you consciously choose not to vilify or disparage. You place it in cold storage in your mind, preserving the basic human respect. )
