/Title (Surface thinking assumes that if results are not immediate, then effort is being wasted and direction must be changed. Depth thinking understands that meaningful structures often take time to form, even when progress cannot be measured day by day. The individual who invests modestly but consistently over many years often surpasses the one who waits endlessly for the perfect moment, the person who builds skills quietly becomes indispensable, and the one who remains calm during uncertainty gains leverage when others act out of fear.       The surface world rewards constant motion and visible effort, but the underwater kingdom rewards mastery and mastery is built slowly, silently, and with sustainability at its core.)
/Dest [14 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 9986 0 R
/Next 10415 0 R
