/Title (What I find valuable is that fishing does not reward constant action; it rewards awareness, timing, and restraint. Sometimes doing less is the most effective choice, and sometimes waiting is not a delay but a strategy. This is very close to how discipline actually works in real life and in finances. Sustainable progress is rarely built through constant movement, but through the ability to pause, assess, and act only when action is justified.)
