10606 0 obj
<<
/Title (Disciplinated by Adrenaline     Discipline is often associated with structure, routines, and consistency, but there is another, less obvious dimension: the discipline of intentionally stepping out of comfort zones and challenging your own limits. Testing your adrenaline periodically is not about recklessness or seeking thrills for the sake of excitement; it is about controlled exposure to situations that make your heart race, your mind focus, and your body fully engaged. It is a deliberate exercise in courage, self-awareness, and adaptability. For example, imagine someone who has always feared public speaking. By slowly increasing the stakes first speaking in front of a small group, then a larger audience, and finally participating in a live-streamed presentation they practice the discipline of facing fear while maintaining control.)
/Dest [78 0 R /Fit]
