/Title (Strength here is not about power over others, but mastery over yourself. Forgiveness is, purely and powerfully, a strategic decision for your own peace and progress. It is the ultimate act of reclaiming your energy. When you hold onto resentment, you are perpetually renting space in your mind to a past event and the person who caused it. You are allowing them to live there, rent-free, diverting your emotional resources, your focus, and your creative power. As Tyler Perry so pointedly observes, "When you haven't forgiven those who have hurt you, you turn back against your future. When you do forgive, you start walking forward." Unforgiveness chains you to a past you cannot change, forcing you to face backwards while life moves on.)
/Dest [114 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 10625 0 R
/Prev 10632 0 R
/Next 10648 0 R
>>
endobj
10639 0 obj
<<
/Title (It allows you to move forward without being held hostage by fear, indecision, or chaos, and it opens the door to opportunities that a lack of structure would have hidden from view. The real power of discipline is revealed when it becomes a natural part of who you are. When your habits, decisions, and mindset align with your long-term vision, freedom ceases to be a distant goal and becomes a lived experience.  Those who embrace discipline as a guiding principle discover that life no longer feels like a series of random events but as a purposeful journey where every step is deliberate, every choice matters, and every moment belongs to them.)
